      "date": "4 September 58 BCE",
      "event_category": "Connected",
      "title": "THE FIRST CONSIGNMENTS OF VALERIUS’S LIBRARY REACH HIS ESTATES",
      "mentioned_entities": [
        "Gaius Maximus Valerius",
        "estate stewards",
        "book carriers",
        "settlement residents"
      ],
      "body": "The first organized consignments from Valerius’s Roman library reach his estates after the journey from Rome. Stewards receive the bundles against written inventories, separating philosophical, historical, rhetorical, poetic, and practical works so that the collection can be used rather than merely stored. The books are placed in protected rooms already under estate administration, and copies are marked according to their assigned collection. Residents and workers are informed that the books may be consulted without a fee or special social standing. The arrival turns the educational project discussed in Rome into a physical institution on Valerius’s own holdings.",
