      ],
      "body": "Quintus Caecilius Metellus Celer sends word to Valerius concerning the continuing interest in the raid evidence. The communication is careful not to claim that the investigation has established more than the surviving evidence supports, but it indicates that the matter remains known among Roman political correspondents. Valerius’s account of the wax seal and the testimony of the captured men is now part of a longer chain of correspondence rather than an isolated report. Celer also asks whether Valerius has received any further communication from the regional authority. The exchange keeps the investigation connected to the political relationships Valerius established in Rome.",
