      "date": "30 September 58 BCE",
      "event_category": "Connected",
      "title": "VALERIUS’S ESTATE READERS BEGIN ASKING FOR COPIES OF THE MOST USED TEXTS",
      "mentioned_entities": [
        "Gaius Maximus Valerius",
        "estate readers",
        "copyists",
        "estate stewards"
      ],
      "body": "By the end of the month, the stewards report that several works in the new reading rooms are being requested repeatedly. Readers begin asking whether copies can be made locally so that the most useful texts do not remain tied to a single physical volume. Valerius authorizes the stewards to identify the works most frequently requested and begin arranging careful copies where qualified scribes can be found. The proposal expands the educational project beyond simply transporting his Roman collection to the estates. It also creates a practical connection between the books, the people using them, and the skilled labor required to reproduce them.",
